{"ts": "2026-07-30T08:54:34.133+00:00", "event": "request", "attempt": 1, "n_messages": 1, "roles": ["user"], "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Create a command-line tool `wordstats.py` in your workspace.\n\nUsage: `python wordstats.py <path-to-text-file>`\n\nIt must print exactly three lines to stdout:\n\n```\nlines: <number of lines in the file>\nwords: <total word count>\ntop: <word> <count>\n```\n\nDefinitions:\n- A *word* is a maximal run of ASCII letters (`a`–`z`) after lowercasing the\n  whole text. Digits, punctuation and underscores separate words.\n- `lines` is the number of lines in the file (as split by newline; a trailing\n  final newline does not add an extra line).\n- `top` is the most frequent word and its count. Ties are broken alphabetically\n  (earliest wins). If the file has no words, print `top: - 0`.\n\nCreate the file, then test it yourself against a sample file before finishing.\n"}]}
{"ts": "2026-07-30T08:54:49.063+00:00", "event": "response", "attempt": 1, "text": "", "stop_reason": "tool_calls", "tokens_in": 837, "tokens_out": 372, "reasoning_tokens": null, "total_ms": 14929.2, "ttft_ms": null, "cost_usd": null, "served_by": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "QBpOl4St0nEZBZXyd7q4xxGOG4oUdwwD", "name": "write_file", "args": {"path": "wordstats.py", "content": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport sys\nimport re\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef main():\n    if len(sys.argv) != 2:\n        print(\"Usage: python wordstats.py <path-to-text-file>\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n    \n    filepath = sys.argv[1]\n    \n    with open(filepath, 'r', encoding='ascii') as f:\n        content = f.read()\n    \n    # Count lines (split by newline; trailing newline doesn't add extra line)\n    if content == '':\n        num_lines = 0\n    else:\n        num_lines = len(content.split('\\n'))\n        # If file ends with newline, don't count the empty string after last newline as a line\n        if content.endswith('\\n'):\n            num_lines -= 1\n    \n    # Extract words: maximal runs of ASCII letters after lowercasing\n    text_lower = content.lower()\n    words = re.findall(r'[a-z]+', text_lower)\n    \n    word_count = len(words)\n    \n    if word_count == 0:\n        top_word = '-'\n        top_count = 0\n    else:\n        counter = Counter(words)\n        max_count = max(counter.values())\n        # Get all words with max count, then sort alphabetically\n        top_words = sorted([w for w, c in counter.items() if c == max_count])\n        top_word = top_words[0]\n        top_count = max_count\n    \n    print(f\"lines: {num_lines}\")\n    print(f\"words: {word_count}\")\n    print(f\"top: {top_word} {top_count}\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n"}}]}
